## Context
Raid 3d5ae7, PR #2114 (2026-10-31). Gate round 1 REROLLed on 9b70c368. The fix commit was rebased onto origin/main, as `rules/git.md` requires before every gate, giving 5f13e765. Round 2 was refused at admission: `scripts/review_notes.py` `gate_state` (reroll-fix branch, about line 913) admits a round-2 head only when the rerolled head is its ancestor (`merge-base --is-ancestor`), which a rebase never satisfies. `git range-diff` showed the three reviewed commits identical. Workaround used: a delta re-gaze on the rebased head, then round 2 was admitted and APPROVED.

The two rules contradict: following "rebase before every gate" makes the reroll-fix admission unreachable, and each rebased fix costs one extra gaze.

## Scope
Admit a round-2 head when the rerolled head is its ancestor OR its commits since the merge base are patch-equivalent (patch-id, as `coverage()` already uses) to the rerolled range plus new commits.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] A test: reroll on head A, rebase A's commits onto a moved base and add a fix commit; `gate_state` admits it as `reroll-fix`
- [ ] A test: a rebased head whose earlier commits changed content is still refused

## Imagine (raid 1f0534)
- Premise holds on 2a5547b8: `scripts/review_notes.py:915` admits reroll-fix only when the rerolled head is an ancestor.
- Simplest path: OR the ancestor test with patch-equivalence of the rerolled range (merge-base..A) against the new range, reusing the patch-id helper `coverage()` already has; no new git plumbing.
- Antipatterns: none; do not add a range-diff dependency.

## Feasibility (raid 1f0534)
- PASS. `gate_state` :875, reroll-fix :914-916. No per-commit patch-id helper exists: `_binding` (:618-627) hashes the whole range; per-commit equivalence needs `git cherry` or per-commit `patch-id`. Check the rerolled head's objects survive a force-push on a fresh gate host (are verdict heads pinned under refs/review-heads, :116, like answer heads?).
